{
  "uid": "morph-engine",
  "title": "Desire Path — the adaptive engine",
  "description": "What the bandit is doing and whether it should be trusted. A bandit fails quietly, so most of these panels are about detecting a system that looks healthy and has stopped learning.",
  "tags": ["morph", "engine", "bandit"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": false,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-7d",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timepicker": {
    "refresh_intervals": ["1m", "5m", "15m", "1h"]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "The claim",
      "description": "One number decides whether any of the rest was worth building: does the adapting site beat the un-adapting one. Everything else on this dashboard explains that number rather than replacing it.",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "gauge",
      "title": "Lift over the holdout cohort",
      "description": "The 5% of visitors pinned to the baseline are the control group, and this is the measured difference against them. It is the only honest statement of value the system can make, because it compares against itself rather than against a guess or a memory of how the old site performed. Reported hourly with an always-valid p-value, so watching it continuously does not inflate the false-positive rate the way peeking at a fixed-horizon test would.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "morph_holdout_lift_relative",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "max": 1,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#f5c15e",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": 0.05
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showThresholdLabels": false,
        "showThresholdMarkers": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Has the lift held up over time?",
      "description": "A single reading can be luck. The trend is what distinguishes a system that is learning from one that got a good week — and a lift that decays steadily towards zero is the signature of a bandit that has stopped exploring and is riding a variant the audience has moved past.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "morph_holdout_lift_relative",
          "legendFormat": "lift vs holdout",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Is it still able to learn?",
      "description": "A bandit fails quietly. It keeps serving pages, keeps reporting a healthy reward, and simply loses the ability to notice that the world changed — which looks exactly like success until the day it is not.",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "gauge",
      "title": "Exploration rate against its floor",
      "description": "Share of impressions going to something other than the current leader. The 2% floor exists because Thompson sampling self-anneals: exploration shrinks as evidence accumulates, and without a floor it shrinks to nothing. Measured from impressions actually served rather than from the configured floor, because the configured floor is the intent and this is the outcome — the whole point is to catch them diverging.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "morph_exploration_rate",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "max": 0.2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#f5c15e",
                "value": 0.005
              },
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": 0.02
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showThresholdLabels": false,
        "showThresholdMarkers": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Exploration over time, against the 2% floor",
      "description": "Watch for a slow decline rather than a cliff. Exponential forgetting caps the pseudo-count so a posterior can always be moved, but a surface that has lost every variant except its leader has nothing left to explore with — and that shows up here as a floor breach without anything having gone wrong.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 10
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "morph_exploration_rate",
          "legendFormat": "exploration",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": 0.02
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "What is it changing, and is it keeping up?",
      "description": "The adapt job folds one hour of evidence into the posteriors every hour. When it falls behind, the site carries on serving the last decision set it managed to publish — correctly, and with no outward sign.",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Hours behind",
      "description": "Now, minus the last hour folded into the posteriors. One hour is normal — the job processes the hour that has just finished. Two or more means it is falling behind or has stopped, and the site is adapting on conclusions that are getting older by the hour.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(time() - max(morph_adapt_cycle_hour_seconds)) / 3600",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "h",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#f5c15e",
                "value": 2
              },
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": 4
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Removed in the last day",
      "description": "Retirements plus quarantines over 24 hours. Zero for days on a site with traffic usually means the guardrails are not reaching their evidence thresholds rather than that every variant is good — check the impression counts before concluding the pool is healthy.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 19
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "increase(morph_variants_retired_total[24h]) + increase(morph_variants_quarantined_total[24h])",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Retirements versus quarantines",
      "description": "Two mechanisms that mean different things and are deliberately not merged. A retirement is the reward statistics settling against a variant — the system working. A quarantine is the health guardrail removing something that was harming Core Web Vitals, client errors or bounce rate, on a signal the reward cannot see. A burst of quarantines is a deploy that broke something; a trickle of retirements is a Tuesday.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 19
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "increase(morph_variants_retired_total[6h])",
          "legendFormat": "retired (reward settled)",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "increase(morph_variants_quarantined_total[6h])",
          "legendFormat": "quarantined (health breach)",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Is the decision cheap enough to keep making?",
      "description": "Adaptation that costs more than it returns is a worse site with extra steps. §7 budgets the decision at 5 ms and the page at 150 ms TTFB, and both have to hold on every render, not on average.",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 26
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Decision latency distribution",
      "description": "p50, p95 and p99 together, because the shape matters more than any one line. The three tracking each other is a healthy path; p99 detaching while p50 holds is contention, usually on the snapshot cache refresh rather than in the maths.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum(rate(morph_decision_duration_ms_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(morph_decision_duration_ms_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum(rate(morph_decision_duration_ms_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": 5
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "How stale is the decision set the renderer is serving?",
      "description": "Measured at the renderer rather than at the worker that wrote it, and that distinction is the point: a worker convinced it published fifteen minutes ago while a renderer still holds yesterday is exactly the disagreement worth being able to see. A sawtooth climbing to an hour and dropping is the job working. A monotonic climb is Redis, the worker, or the wire between them.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 27
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "morph_snapshot_age_seconds",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}} snapshot age",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#6ef3c8",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#f5c15e",
                "value": 7200
              },
              {
                "color": "#ff6b6b",
                "value": 14400
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "gradientMode": "opacity"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
